WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.320
The gateway must never reach the secret store:

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.660
not directly, and not through another service.

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:09.310
In Shape, connections are relations you declare.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.760
Gateway calls Policy Service.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.440
Policy Service provides the Secret Store.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.630
The check passes: nothing forbids that yet.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.800
So add a rule:

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.930
no path from Gateway to Secret

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.240
Store over calls or provides.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.840
The check walks the declared graph

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:28.290
and fails with a forbidden path.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.480
The witness names each relation on the route,

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.610
so you know which link to break.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.460
Rules can also allow just

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.240
one provider for an endpoint, or forbid dependency cycles.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.750
Shape sees only the relations you declare;

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.820
it never reads your code.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.630
So review keeps the graph honest,

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:48.490
and shp graph show lets you inspect it.
